1. Ng6+ Kg8 2. e5 Bg4 3. Ne3 $1 (3. Nfxe7+ $2 Kf7 4. Kd8 (4. Nxh8+ Kxe7 $10)
4... Bg7 $10)  (3. Nh6+ $2 Kg7 4. Nxg4 Kxg6 $10) 3... Bh3 $1 (3... Be6 4. Nxh8
Kxh8 (4... d6+ 5. Kd8 $18) 5. Kd8 Kg7 (5... d6 6. Kxe7 $18) 6. Kxe7 $18)  (3...
Bh5 4. Nxh8 $18) 4. Nf4 $1 {switchback}  (4. Kd8 $2 Bg7 $10)  (4. Nxh8 d6+ 5.
Kd8 Kxh8 6. Kxe7 (6. exd6 exd6 $10) 6... dxe5 $10) 4... Be6 {the only square
for the bishop}  (4... Bxe5 5. Nxh3 $18) 5. Nxe6 dxe6 6. Nc4 $1 (6. d4 $2 Kf7
7. Kd7 Bg7 8. Ng4 (8. Ng2 Bh6 $10) 8... Bf8 $10)  (6. Kd7 $2 Bxe5 $10) 6... Kf8
(6... Bg7 7. d3 $1 Kf8 8. Kd8 $1 {leads to the mainline} ) 7. Kd8 $1 (7. Kd7 $2
Bg7 $1 8. Kxe6 Ke8 9. d3 Bh6 $1 $10)  (7. d4 $2 Bg7 8. Kd7 Bh6 9. Kxe6 Ke8 $10)
7... Bg7 8. d3 $1 (8. Kd7 $2 Bh6 $10 {see above} ) 8... Kf7 (8... Bh6 9. Na5 $1
Bf4 10. Nc6 Kf7 11. Kd7 $1 Bg5 12. Nd8+ $18) 9. Kd7 Bh8 (9... Bh6 10. Na5 $1
$18)  (9... Bf8 10. Na5 $1 $18) 10. d4 Bg7 11. Nd6+ $1 (11. Na5 $2 Bh6 12. Nc6
Be3 $1 13. Nd8+ Kg6 14. Nxe6 (14. Kxe6 Bxd4 $10) 14... Kf5 15. Kxe7 Bxd4 16.
Nxd4+ Kxe5 $10) 11... exd6 (11... Kg6 12. Kxe7 $18) 12. d5 $1 {Irrespective of
how Black continues, White will promote to a queen on e8} 1-0

[Event "The Problemist"]
[ECO "A00"]
[Annotator "? "]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "?"]
[Date "2026.09.??"]
[Round "?"]
[White "Hergert=V Neuenschwander=B"]
[Black "(=0041.35h2d1)"]
[Result "1/2-1/2"]
[FEN "8/p4p2/Pp1pp2B/8/4P3/4P1N1/1b5K/3k4 w - - 0 1"]
1. Bg5 $1 {It is crucial to threaten 2.Bd8 and 3.Bxb6 to provoke the f-pawn's
advance, which weakens the pawn on e6.}  (1. e5 $2 Bxe5 $19)  (1. Bf4 $2 Be5 2.
Bxe5 dxe5 3. Nh5 b5 $19 {no Ng7xe6} )  (1. Bf8 $2 Be5 $19) 1... f6 (1... Be5 $4
2. Bd8 $1 b5 3. Ba5 $1 $18) 2. Bf4 Ba3 (2... Be5 {leads to the main line} )  (
2... e5 3. Bh6 b5 4. Nf5 $11) 3. Bh6 $1 (3. Nh5 $2 b5 4. Nxf6 e5 5. Bg3 b4 $19)
3... Bb2 4. Bf4 Be5 5. Bxe5 (5. Nh5 $2 b5 6. Nxf6 b4 $1 $19) 5... dxe5 (
{Stronger than} 5... fxe5 {after which White has different ways to draw, e.g.,}
6. Nf5) 6. Nh5 b5 7. Ng7 $1 {First thematic try:}  (7. Nxf6 $2 b4 8. Nd5 b3 $1
9. Nc3+ Kc1 $1 10. Nb5 b2 11. Na3 b1=Q 12. Nxb1 Kxb1 $19 {In comparison to the
main line, White cannot draw with 13.Kh1 (opposition) because the black king
has time to capture the a6 pawn.} ) 7... b4 8. Nxe6 {In contrast to the 7.Nxf6
line, Black pawn structure (f6/e5 instead of e6/e5) gives White's king access
to the square f5, making Black's plan to attack the a6 pawn too slow.} 8... b3
9. Nc7 $1 {Second thematic try:}  (9. Nc5 $2 b2 10. Na4 Kc1 11. Nxb2 Kxb2 $19
{White managed to eliminate the passed pawn, but loses the opposition.} ) 9...
b2 10. Nb5 Kc1 (10... b1=Q 11. Nc3+ Kc1 12. Nxb1 Kxb1 {leads to the main line}
) 11. Na3 b1=Q 12. Nxb1 Kxb1 13. Kh1 $1 {Now it is Black to move!} 13... Kc1
14. Kg1 Kd1 15. Kf1 Kc2 16. Kg2 $1 (16. Ke2 $2 Kc3 $19 {White loses the
opposition.} ) 16... Kd2 17. Kf2 Kc3 18. Kg3 Kd3 19. Kf3 Kc4 20. Kg4 Kb5 21.
Kf5 Kxa6 22. Kxf6 Kb6 23. Kxe5 $11 1/2-1/2

