against one bishop.}  (1... Kf6 $2 2. Ng4+ $18) 2. c8=N+ $1 (2. c8=Q $2 Be6+ 3.
Qxe6+ Kxe6 $10 {because Black's pawn is advanced too far} ) 2... Kd7 {In the
sequel Black must play actively because three knights win against one bishop.}
3. Nb6+ Kc6 4. Na4 Kb5 5. Nc3+ Kb4 6. Ne2 c3 {Mobilizing the passed pawn is
Black's best resource.} 7. Ne3 $1 (7. Ne1 $2 Bc4 $1 8. Nf4 (8. Nc1 c2 $10)  (8.
Nd4 Kc5 9. Nhf3 Bd5 $10) 8... Kb3 9. Nhf3 c2 10. Nd4+ Kc3 11. Ndxc2 Kd2 12. Kg3
Bb3 $10) 7... Bc4 8. Nf4 Kb3 (8... Bb3 9. Nd3+ Ka3 10. Nf3 $18) 9. Nf3 c2 10.
